ixel's position within the larger block's structure seems to be the key determinant.\n\n**Locating Box Position**\n\nI've determined the 5x5 box resides in the bottom-right corner. Analyzing the 3x3 interior within this, I see distinct, unconnected non-zero cells. Each of these cells, when scaled by four, forms a 4x4 block in the output, with their color defining the border of that scaled block.\n\n**Refining Pixel Logic**\n\nI've confirmed that the color '2' originates from a specific 1x1 pixel within the 2x2 interior of each scaled block. This 1x1 pixel is always the bottom-right one, and its position relative to the overall block structure is key to understanding the color assignments.\n\n",
